### One process note worth flagging
The Step 7 subagent's per-iteration `rm -f` left no persisted results files on exit (a known gotcha), so I re-ran the sweep to regenerate and independently verify. My **first** re-run used `--start-command "bash start.sh"` (outer `cd` only) and produced a false-alarm total failure — all 65 tests ERRORed with *"could not be restarted"* because per-test restarts spawn from pytest's rootdir, not the impl dir. That's the documented start-command cwd gotcha, **not** an implementation bug. Re-running with `cd <impl> && bash start.sh` embedded confirmed a clean 65/65 across all 8 rounds. The implementation was correct the whole time.

